&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique role bespoke to the Nike EMEA Affiliate Program. The Senior Account Manager, Influencers &amp;amp; Campaigns is responsible for the day-to-day management, planning, and execution of Nike&#39;s creator and content affiliate marketing activity across the UK &amp;amp; supporting EMEA markets.&lt;br&gt;Acting as the key operational lead, this role oversees the end-to-end delivery of both Nike brand campaigns and evergreen/ always-on creator workstreams, ensuring all activations are executed seamlessly and aligned to Nike&#39;s strategic, commercial, and brand objectives.&lt;br&gt;The role manages creator partnerships across the affiliate programme, leads creator network relationships, and coordinates cross-functional stakeholders to bring campaigns to life from briefing and talent selection through to activation, reporting, and optimisation.&lt;br&gt;This role works closely with the Global Client Strategy Lead and Nike, along with internal teams, and external partners. The Senior Account Manager ensures creator activity drives measurable business results while maintaining a premium brand experience and strong operational excellence.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Tasks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the end-to-end delivery of Nike creator campaigns across multiple EMEA markets, from creator sourcing and briefing through to activation, optimisation and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the day-to-day running of affiliate creator programmes, including creator sourcing, recruitment, approvals and ongoing programme engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate campaign execution across Nike stakeholders, internal teams and external partners, ensuring clear communication of briefs, deliverables and timelines, while providing regular campaign status updates to the client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee creator agreements, usage and exclusivity rights across campaigns, ensuring terms are clearly documented and agreed with creators and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and maintain strong relationships with creators, agencies, influencer networks and Nike stakeholders across multiple markets, supporting effective collaboration and campaign delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee campaign budgets across multiple markets, managing commission rates and fixed fees to ensure timely and accurate compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the end-to-end affiliate creator journey and linking capabilities across social platforms, including how different content placements and link formats drive traffic back to Nike.com and enable performance tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate and manage unique campaign tracking links and click refs, ensuring activity can be accurately tracked, attributed and reported against campaign KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor campaign performance and develop post-campaign analysis reports, presenting actionable insights and recommendations to key channel stakeholders to inform future activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and maintain creator onboarding documents, content guidelines and dos and don’ts, ensuring Nike brand standards are upheld, and guidance evolves based on campaign feedback, approval learnings and best practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the global point of contact and subject matter expert for creator activity, partnering closely with teams across Nike EMEA programmes to support planning, execution, best practice and partner recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support seasonal planning and campaign development across key brand, product and commercial moments, using creator, platform and industry insights to shape recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and develop creator resources across Nike EMEA Affiliate Programmes, including the Affiliate Playbook and Creator Recruitment Guidelines, helping streamline onboarding, ensure consistent programme understanding and drive active engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the wider Global Account Management department with Influencer/Creator initiatives, providing support to internal teams and clients where required, advising on best practices, process development etc&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Expertise&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Professional experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing complex affiliate, creator programmes for global brands, overseeing planning, activation, optimisation, and performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the delivery of integrated campaigns across affiliate, content &amp;amp; creator channels, ensuring alignment with both commercial and brand objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building strong relationships with clients, publishers, creators, agencies, and technology partners to drive programme growth and unlock new opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing strategic recommendations based on market trends, performance data, and industry developments, helping&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Personal skills:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organised with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-builder, able to establish trusted partnerships with clients, partners, and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, confident engaging and influencing stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and solutions-focused, taking ownership and driving initiatives forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
