&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your onboarding&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll&amp;nbsp;participate&amp;nbsp;in&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ONPObMHh-k8&quot;&gt;Global Optiver Academy&lt;/a&gt;, a structured&amp;nbsp;onboarding programme for graduates. It gives new joiners a shared foundation in how Optiver trades, builds systems, and manages risk before they move into their teams.&amp;nbsp;As part of your onboarding,&amp;nbsp;you&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;gain exposure to the AI tools and technologies that support research and development across the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the team you join, you&#39;ll own the research end to end. That could include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building models for pricing, forecasting and signal discovery, choosing the statistical, mathematical or Machine Learning methods that best fit the problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working across petabytes of market, order-flow and unstructured data to find signals that improve strategies as conditions change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring models in production and using live behavior to refine your assumptions and decide what to investigate next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using deep learning and AI-enabled workflows to shorten the loop from hypothesis to evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working directly with researchers, traders and engineers to shape problems and understand how system constraints affect performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for aspiring Quantitative Researchers who are versatile and creative in innovating and suggesting new solutions. In return, we&#39;ll give you the freedom to pursue your ideas and implement them right into our production systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In terms of skills and qualifications, we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An academic degree in Engineering, Physics, Maths, Econometrics, Computer science or equivalent, with outstanding academic achievements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in any language (preferably Python, but C, C++, Basic, JAVA, etc. are also a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to apply concepts of probability, calculus and linear algebra&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive attitude and eagerness to constantly improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written English language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a culture of collaboration and excellence, where you’ll be surrounded by curious thinkers and creative problem solvers. Motivated by a passion for continuous improvement, you’ll thrive in a supportive, high-performing environment alongside talent colleagues, working collaboratively to tackle the toughest problems in the financial markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition, you’ll receive:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A performance-based bonus structure, enabling all of our employees to benefit from our global profit pool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to work alongside best-in-class professionals from over 50 countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 paid vacation days in your first year, increasing to 30 from your second year onwards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training opportunities, discounts on health benefits, and fully paid first-class commuting expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive office perks, including breakfast, lunch and dinner, world-class barista coffee, bi-weekly chair massages, Friday afternoon drinks, a bicycle to explore Amsterdam and much more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training and continuous learning opportunities, including access to conferences and tech events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive relocation packages and visa sponsorship where necessary for expats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOW TO REGISTER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you interested in furthering your career on one of the most dynamic and exciting trading floors in Europe?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Complete the short form below with your details and upload your CV in English. Registering your interest is not a job application, and it does not start an assessment process. We&#39;ll contact you when we have opportunities that match your profile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kindly note that we do not require any assistance from third-parties including agencies in the recruitment of this role. If you have any questions feel free to contact our Recruitment team via our &lt;a href=&quot;https://optiver.com/contact-eu-recruitment/&quot;&gt;recruitment inquiry form.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Optiver is committed to &lt;a href=&quot;https://optiver.com/diversity-statement/&quot;&gt;diversity and inclusion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We encourage applications from candidates from any and all backgrounds, and we welcome requests for reasonable adjustments during the process to ensure that you can best demonstrate your abilities. Please let us know if you would like to request any reasonable adjustments by contacting the Recruitment team via the &lt;a href=&quot;https://optiver.com/contact-eu-recruitment&quot;&gt;contact form&lt;/a&gt;, selecting &quot;Reasonable Adjustments&quot; as the subject of your inquiry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For answers to some of our most frequently asked questions, refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.optiver.com/join-us/stories/optiver-europe-recruitment-faq/&quot;&gt;recruitment FAQ&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For applicants based in India, our entry route is via the placement office internship hiring season (July/August).&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;At Graviton, we don&#39;t believe the best trading strategies come from following established playbooks. They come from asking better questions. Why does a pattern exist? What is driving it? Is it real or just noise? Can it be explained, modelled and turned into an edge?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Quantitative Researcher, you&#39;ll work on those questions every day. You&#39;ll investigate market behaviour, develop quantitative models, build and test hypotheses and turn insights into trading strategies, working alongside researchers and technologists in an environment where an idea on a whiteboard can reach live trading quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t a role where the answers are in a textbook. The problems are open-ended, the data is enormous, and finding the answers is the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates are rigorous thinkers who genuinely enjoy mathematics, programming and figuring out things that aren&#39;t obvious, based in our Singapore, London, Amsterdam or US offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Work On&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work across quantitative research and systematic trading, taking ideas through the full lifecycle: question, hypothesis, experiment, model, validation, strategy, production. Depending on your team and research interests, your work would include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discovering predictive patterns and sources of alpha from billions of market events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulating hypotheses about market behaviour and designing experiments to test them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying probability, statistics, optimization and machine learning to build predictive models and quantitative signals for systematic trading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing robust backtests and statistical tests to distinguish genuine signals from noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with large and complex datasets to uncover patterns that aren&#39;t immediately visible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating market microstructure and how markets behave at different timescales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluating strategy performance, identifying weaknesses and continuously refining models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing research infrastructure and AI-powered tools and agents that make experimentation faster and analysis deeper&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with technologists to translate research ideas into efficient, production-ready systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exploring new techniques in machine learning, statistics and quantitative finance to uncover new sources of edge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No two research problems are the same. Good research finds patterns. Great research understands why they exist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Successful researchers at Graviton discover new sources of alpha and turn them into robust trading strategies, build models that hold up under real market conditions and not only in backtests, develop a deep understanding of market behaviour, create research frameworks and tools that make the broader team more effective, work with technologists to take ideas from research into production, and communicate complex quantitative ideas clearly and rigorously. Your impact isn&#39;t measured by how many models you build. It&#39;s measured by the quality of the ideas you discover and what those ideas enable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for exceptional problem solvers who genuinely enjoy mathematics, programming and figuring out things that aren&#39;t obvious.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in a quantitative discipline such as mathematics, physics, computer science, statistics, operations research or machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No active backlogs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python and/or C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grounding in probability, statistics, linear algebra and optimization, with experience in machine learning, statistical modelling or data analysis, whether through coursework, research or personal projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with large, complex datasets, and strong analytical thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for applying quantitative thinking and rigorous research to solve open-ended problems in markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain complex ideas clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior exposure to quantitative research, algorithmic trading, market microstructure, competitive mathematics or machine learning is valuable, but we care more about how you think than whether you&#39;ve worked in finance before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than specific tools or techniques, we care how you think. We look for people who are curious enough to keep asking why, analytical enough to separate signal from noise, persistent enough to pursue difficult problems, intellectually honest enough to abandon an idea when the evidence says so, and humble enough to keep learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Graviton, researchers sit alongside technologists on specialized trading teams that operate with significant autonomy. You&#39;ll have meaningful ownership of research problems from day one: forming your own hypotheses, challenging existing approaches and following the evidence wherever it leads, with the infrastructure and datasets to test ideas at scale, competitive compensation, and a culture where the best idea wins regardless of who proposed it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Markets are among the most complex systems humans have ever created, and they never stop changing. Neither should our thinking. Every day, someone asks a better question and finds an answer nobody had. That someone could be you.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink, QGroundControl or mission planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UAV flight testing and validation in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with datalinks and radio systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous customer-facing or field engineering role, especially with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;At Jamf, we believe in an open, flexible culture based on respect and trust. Our track record and thriving work environment all stem from the freedom we grant ourselves to get the job done right. We take pride in helping tens of thousands of customers around the globe succeed with Apple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The secret to our success lies in our connectivity, while operating with a high degree of flexibility. Work-life balance remains our priority while feeling connected is important to maintain our strong culture, achieve our goals, and thrive as #OneJamf.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do at Jamf:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Enterprise New Logo Account Executive MEA &lt;/strong&gt;is a results-driven hunter responsible for identifying, pursuing, and closing new enterprise logos for Jamf. Focused exclusively on net-new acquisition within the enterprise segment (organizations with 1,000+ employees), this role requires strong prospecting discipline, the ability to manage complex multi-stakeholder sales cycles, and the consultative acumen to position Jamf&#39;s Apple Enterprise Management solutions at the executive level. Success in this role is defined by consistent pipeline generation, new logo attainment, and laying the foundation for long-term customer partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is offered in &lt;strong&gt;The Netherlands only&lt;/strong&gt;, preferably for candidates located in the Randstad and used to travel to MEA&amp;nbsp;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What you can expect to do this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Logo Prospecting &amp;amp; Pipeline Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a targeted outbound prospecting motion to identify and engage net-new enterprise accounts within an assigned segment or territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop segment fluency — understanding buyer personas, common objections, industry-specific compliance needs, and Apple ecosystem maturity within target accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing, Business Development, and Channel partners to execute coordinated account-based prospecting that feeds a healthy, qualified pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain consistent pipeline coverage and hygiene, ensuring sufficient volume and stage diversity to meet and exceed quota targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Sales Cycle Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full sales cycle from initial outreach and discovery through proposal, negotiation, and close — navigating the complexity typical of enterprise buying processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and engage multiple stakeholders across IT, Security, Finance, Legal, Procurement, and executive leadership to build multi-threaded relationships within target accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply a structured qualification methodology (e.g., MEDDPICC) to assess deal health, prioritize effort, and improve forecast accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate enterprise procurement processes, including security reviews, DPAs, and SLAs, with support from Jamf Legal and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver compelling business cases, demonstrations, and ROI presentations tailored to the priorities of diverse buying audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Deal Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure initial commercial agreements that are competitive, value-aligned, and appropriately sized to facilitate a strong land — with long-term expansion in mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate contract terms with support from Jamf Legal and Finance, maintaining deal momentum while protecting Jamf&#39;s commercial interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain competitive positioning in deals where incumbents or alternatives are present; articulate Jamf&#39;s differentiated value with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner &amp;amp; Ecosystem Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build productive working relationships with Apple&#39;s enterprise sales team and Jamf&#39;s channel and reseller partners to generate introductions and support deal execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage partner resources appropriately to accelerate pipeline and strengthen account access, especially within named accounts or complex organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forecasting, Reporting &amp;amp; Team Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate, up-to-date records in Salesforce, including account activity, pipeline stage, and deal notes, to support individual and team forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide consistent, reliable monthly and quarterly forecasts, with clear visibility into deal status and expected close timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share learnings from the field — win/loss patterns, competitive intelligence, objection themes — to contribute to team and segment knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5 years of B2B SaaS or technology sales experience with a demonstrated track record of meeting or exceeding quota (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional working proficiency in English is required and Arabic is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex enterprise sales cycles involving multiple stakeholders, including IT and executive-level buyers (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to generate pipeline through outbound prospecting, partner engagement, and marketing collaboration (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a structured sales qualification methodology (e.g., MEDDPICC, MEDDIC, SPIN) and ability to apply it to assess deal health (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively in both direct and indirect (channel/partner) selling models (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills; able to deliver clear and persuasive presentations to technical and business audiences (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Salesforce or equivalent CRM for pipeline tracking, forecasting, and activity documentation (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consultative, solutions-oriented selling approach with the ability to connect technology to business outcomes (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Apple enterprise ecosystem, endpoint management, or SaaS security solutions (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating enterprise procurement processes including DPAs, SLAs, and security reviews (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed and resilient; able to manage long sales cycles and ambiguous buying processes with discipline and focus (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel in the MEA territory around 40%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SECURITY AND PRIVACY REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;markedContent&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in ongoing security training is mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established security protocols will be adhered to, sensitive data will be handled responsibly, and data protection practices are followed, including understanding relevant privacy regulations and reporting breaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acknowledging the Jamf Code of Conduct, where applicable security and privacy policies can be found, is a requirement of all roles at Jamf.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Why Jamf?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Named a Fortune Best Workplace for Millennials, 2021.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;We offer a clear and defined sales career path. Our main goal is to help you successfully step into our Account Executive role, but there are many ways to advance your career at Jamf.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;We train and then we give you the room to grow. Our Jamfs can explore the vertical career path, as well as the horizontal, to discover new interests and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;You don’t have to be a techie to be a Jamf. Our best-in-class sales focused Bootcamp training provides you with the technical and product knowledge required to confidently talk with customers about Jamf.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;We set achievable targets, help each other out, and share best practices across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;You will have the opportunity to make a real and meaningful impact for more than 70,000 global customers with the best Apple device management solution in the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;We put people over profits – which is why our customers keep coming back to us.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;We encourage you to simply be you. We constantly seek and value different perspectives to ensure Jamf is a place where everyone feels comfortable and can be successful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;23 of 25 world’s most valuable brands rely on Jamf to do their best work (as ranked by Forbes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it means to be a Jamf?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We are a team of free-thinkers, can-doers, and problem-crushers. We value humility and the relentless pursuit of knowledge. Our culture flows from a spirit of selflessness and relentless self-improvement - driving both personal growth and collective progress throughout our company. We unite around common goals while respecting personal approaches, believing that fulfilled individuals create a thriving, vibrant workplace.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our aim is simple: hire exceptionally good people who are incredibly good at what they do and let them do it. We provide the support and resources to let everyone be their authentic, best selves at work, at rest, and at play. We are committed to supporting the continual improvement of Apple in the workplace, the organizations that rely on them and the people who keep it all running smoothly.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Above it all, waves our banner of #OneJamf – and the knowledge that when we stand together, we accomplish so much more than we could alone. We seek individuals who share this unwavering journey toward growth to join us in our quest for constant improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does Jamf do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Jamf extends the legendary Apple experience people enjoy in their personal lives to the workplace. We believe the experience of using a device at work or school should feel the same, and be as secure as, using a personal device.&amp;nbsp;With Jamf, customers are able to confidently automate Mac, iPad, iPhone and Apple TV deployment, management, and security – anytime, anywhere – to protect the data and applications used by employees in the workplace, students learning in the classroom, and streamline communications in healthcare between patients and providers.&amp;nbsp;More than 2,500 Jamf strong worldwide, we are free-thinkers, can-doers, and problems crushers who are encouraged to bring their whole selves to work each and every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get social with us and follow the conversation at #OneJamf&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
